===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|cunte}}, {{m|enm|queynt}}, {{m|enm|queynte}}, from {{inh|en|ang|*cunte}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*kuntǭ}}. Cognate with {{cog|fy|kunte}}, {{cog|dum|conte}} ({{cog|nl|kont||butt}}), dialectal {{cog|sv|kunta}}, dialectal {{cog|da|kunte}}, and {{cog|is|kunta}}. A relationship to {{cog|la|cunnus}} has not been conclusively shown. [[w:Eric Partridge|Partridge]] suggests {{m|la|cuneus||a wedge}}.

